---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: /growth-charts/
title: Growth Charts
description: Paediatric growth charts for boys and girls from birth to 18 years — plot length or height against percentile curves.
eyebrow: "Paediatric"
lede: "Plot a child's length or height against percentile curves, from birth to 18 years."
---

<div class="section">
  <div class="container">

    {% for group in [
      { label: "Boys", keys: ["boys-0-2", "boys-2-5", "boys-5-18"] },
      { label: "Girls", keys: ["girls-0-2", "girls-2-5", "girls-5-18"] }
    ] %}
      <section {% if not loop.first %}style="margin-top: var(--space-2xl)"{% endif %}>
        <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-lg)">
          <h2 class="section-title">{{ group.label }}</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="grid grid--3 calculators-grid">
          {% for key in group.keys %}
            {% set c = growthCharts[key] %}
            <article class="card card--interactive card--feature tool-card" data-reveal>
              <div class="card__body">
                <p class="tool-card__kicker">{{ group.label }}</p>
                <p class="badge badge--accent">{{ c.ageMin }}–{{ c.ageMax }} {{ c.ageUnit }}</p>
                <h3 class="card__title">
                  <a href="/growth-charts/{{ key | replace('boys-', 'boys-') | replace('girls-', 'girls-') }}-years/">
                    {{ c.chartTitle }}
                  </a>
                </h3>
                <p class="card__text">
                  {{ c.measureLabel | capitalize }}-for-age percentiles, {{ c.bands | keys | length }} curves.
                </p>
                <p class="card__footer"><span class="btn btn--tertiary">Open chart</span></p>
              </div>
            </article>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </section>
    {% endfor %}

    <div class="alert alert--info" style="margin-top: var(--space-2xl)">
      <div class="alert__body">
        <p>
          These charts are a screening aid, not a diagnosis. A single measurement matters far
          less than the trend over time — always discuss concerns with your paediatrician.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
